                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 26 at 12:09AM MDT until September 26 at 2:15AM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "At 1209 AM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy\nrain across the warned area. Between 2 and 3.5 inches of rain have\nfallen. Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible in the\nwarned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban\nareas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nGrady and Wheatland.\n\nFlash flooding is likely along Highway 275 east of Wheatland as well\nas  Highways 209 and 469 near Grady.",
